#{[17592186485842 #edb/ref 1080 "None of the statements are true" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485842 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485842 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c393b44-730a-5f93-9acb-fbe9996ca594" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485911 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485911 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485911 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ebabf65-87a9-50c0-a00e-9f63618f09de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485925 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485925 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485925 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b2c106c-830c-550f-9834-4e30ffa6398f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485957 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485957 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186485957 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "70454c64-8842-5c74-90d5-a65a027e02d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486040 #edb/ref 1080 "I, II, and III" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486040 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486040 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99988b28-0eb3-5cc7-aaa9-88164b97c763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486043 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486043 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486043 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9b5a2ff6-779a-5eee-95b7-e7c15c73d9b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486051 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486051 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486051 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9ff9d9bd-25c1-553b-af23-b5a3804fa12a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486052 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486052 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486052 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a2106cd2-d4c4-5485-bd50-b22dc45d0703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486154 #edb/ref 1080 "III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486154 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486154 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d51926b0-1f7a-5517-b205-7d50c8ea1fd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186485925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186485957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186485925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486249 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "20236f24-a672-571d-8a2d-4eb8e53f4a42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186485830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186485842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186485911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486258 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "399a1def-da95-5c7b-b07c-dd77153c4399" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-94865" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486410 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a linearly independent set in ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n\nII. $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\nIII. $\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$ is a basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e6a690a-1af9-54cd-96d8-6699f35c43cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486410 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis true if and only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ So, the set is linearly independent.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that all linear combinations of \n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\}\n$$\n\nresult in matrices with the entry ${a}_{21}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ can't be written as a linear combination of the set, it can't form a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486458 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486458 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486458 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486458 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$, where $x\\in {R}^{3}$, is a basis of ${R}^{2}$\n\nII. $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},4{b}_{3}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n\nIII. $\\{{c}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486458 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f5e736f9-a7fd-5964-86e8-9e7f4c30d97a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486458 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{2}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}(4{b}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+(4{x}_{3}){b}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},4{b}_{3}\\}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},4{b}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+\\frac{{x}_{3}}{4}(4{b}_{3})\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The set $\\{{c}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$ because the set consists of all the vectors from the basis $C$ written in a different order.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486489 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486489 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7517e0b5-948e-589e-82bc-4f03c404dd2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486489 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486493 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486493 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "863020c7-988a-55d4-89e2-3c40430f3b22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486493 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186244046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486497 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91cfcf29-baa9-52fa-a889-0d9f790d046b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486497 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186244069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486507 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486507 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b752cd7b-1282-56eb-b8ed-21c8bfb9825b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486507 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486522 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486507 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486522 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fc090e22-1e8a-579b-9615-543cf7ef59c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486522 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406883 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
